hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2675","**
Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti, narrated to us 'Ubaydah ibn Humayd, narrated to me 'Umar ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ya'la ibn Murrah al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said:

One day, I was wearing perfume (khaluq), so a friend of mine said to me, ""Let us go to the house."" So I went, performed ghusl (ritual bath), and applied perfume. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to wipe our faces (with his hand). When he approached me, he held his hand away from the perfume. When he finished wiping, he said to me, ""O Ya'la! What made you apply perfume? Have you gotten married?"" I said, ""No."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me, ""Then go and wash it off.""

So I passed by a well and kept falling into it, then I began to rub myself with soil until it was removed. Then I came back. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw me, he said, ""He has returned with good in his religion. O 'Ula, he has repented, and the heavens have rejoiced.""

Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) indeed commanded Ya'la ibn Murrah to wash off the perfume while he was not in ihram, just as he commanded the one in ihram to wash off the perfume."
